# YAML 1.2
# Citation File Format -- https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this file.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Qaiji-IR (开济IR): A Cross-Layer Quantum-Classical Digital-Twin Intermediate Representation"
message: >-
  If you use Qaiji-IR in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file. After the first Zenodo release, prefer the
  version-specific DOI to reference the exact code used.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jun
    family-names: Ye
    email: yjmaxpayne@hotmail.com
    affiliation: Independent
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1963-0865"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yjmaxpayne/Qaiji-IR"
url: "https://yjmaxpayne.github.io/Qaiji-IR/"
abstract: >-
  Qaiji-IR is a cross-layer intermediate representation for hybrid
  quantum-classical computing. It keeps semantic authority inside the IR and
  treats OpenQASM 3, QIR and MLIR as adapter, target and bridge rather than as
  parents. The code base provides a circuit-level front-end model, a
  bidirectional OpenQASM 2/3 codec that loudly rejects unsupported constructs,
  executable basis and phase convention checks, an L4 semantic-preservation
  core, an L5 program IR, and an L2 native-schedule IR with independent
  certification.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - intermediate representation
  - hybrid quantum-classical
  - digital twin
  - OpenQASM
  - quantum compiler
  - pulse-level control
license: Apache-2.0
